  "notes": [
    "This catalog is an audit snapshot, not yet the runtime source of truth.",
    "Natural Automate now shares the fitted profiles' GeoWonders, Natural Ecotones and Cave Depth Habitats source chain; conservative Natural Three Realms remains unchanged.",
    "The six fitted morphology kernels are internal components of Natural Automate; their standalone world-preset IDs are hidden and retained for compatibility/diagnostics. Kernel suitability tests do not substitute for full multi-seed terrain-quality validation.",
    "Measured DEM profiles are read-only and remain hidden from the ordinary Create World menu.",
    "The current multi-seed workflow exercises internal tva_alpine_three_realms and tva_canyon_three_realms smoothed QA profiles, not the public alpine_three_realms and canyon_three_realms fitted profiles. Do not count those internal runs as direct validation of the public fitted presets.",
    "The current Terrain Lab's legacy `landscape`/`alpine`/`canyon` blend families are a separate model from the six `TerrainArchetypeDensity` fitted families. The public Alpine and Canyon names therefore refer to different algorithms in the old editor and the public preset catalog.",
    "Natural Automate is the sole public Create World preset. It composes the natural baseline with six climate/topography-gated fitted morphology kernels and retains the shared ecology and three-realm dimension stack."
  ]
